    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "The working-hours branch computes both `start` and `end` from `slotStartTime.hour()/minute()`. Because `end` never uses `slotEndTime`, any slot that starts inside working hours will also appear to end inside working hours even when its actual duration extends past `workingHour.endTime`. Before this change, the availability check depended on the full slot interval; after this change, long slots near the boundary can be accepted instead of rejected. For example, a slot starting 10:30 with a 60-minute duration against a 11:00 cutoff should be rejected, but this code compares 10:30 for both start and end and can misclassify it as available.",
      "confidence": 0.7200000286102295,
